## 6. Test module design — `tests/sakg/test_envelope_schema.py`

| Test | Assertion | Guards against |
|---|---|---|
| **T1** | the schema document is itself valid against the draft 2020-12 metaschema (`Draft202012Validator.check_schema`) | a typo'd keyword silently becoming an ignored annotation |
| **T2** | every `valid/*.json` validates cleanly against its manifest profile (parametrised, one test id per fixture) | over-tight schema |
| **T3** | every `invalid/*.json` is rejected **at `manifest.layer`, by `manifest.rule`, at `expect_error_path`** | under-tight schema **and** false-pass fixtures |
| **T4** | manifest ↔ filesystem bijection: every file in `valid/` and `invalid/` has exactly one manifest entry and vice versa | orphan fixtures; phantom entries; a fixture added to inflate the `ls | wc -l` gate |
| **T5** | corpus coverage closure of §5.1: all 12 types, 4 statuses, 4 author_kinds, 3 evidence kinds, both profiles, both nullable fields in both states | silent coverage regression as fixtures evolve |
| **T6** | Layer-2 rules X1–X3 implemented and exercised (also asserts each returns a *named* rule id, not a bare bool) | Layer 2 being quietly dropped |
| **T7** | **format canary** — a document identical to V02 except `ingested_at: "not-a-date"` is rejected; asserts the pattern (not merely `format`) does the work | the draft-2020-12 format-annotation trap |
| **T8** | each of the three named §4.2 invariants maps to ≥ 1 invalid fixture via `manifest.invariant`, and every invariant string is drawn from a closed list | an invariant losing its test during refactor |

Structure notes for IMPLEMENT:

- One module-scope fixture builds the schema and both validators (`authored_node`,
  `stored_node`) once; parametrise over the manifest so pytest reports one test id per
  fixture file (a failure names the offending fixture directly).
- `Draft202012Validator` must be constructed with format checking **enabled**
  (`format_checker=Draft202012Validator.FORMAT_CHECKER`). T7 fails if it is not, but the
  `pattern` keeps Layer 1 correct even if a downstream consumer forgets.
- Layer 2 lives in module-level pure functions `check_x1/x2/x3(doc) -> str | None` returning
  the violated rule id. `I-STORE` imports the same three functions rather than reimplementing
  them (DBT-1 repayment path).
- No network, no `$ref` outside `#/`, no fixture generation at test time — fixtures are
  literal files so they are reviewable and diffable.

