| id | Assumption | Why it is an assumption / verification owner |
|---|---|---|
| **A1** | `sakg/` does not yet exist; `sakg/schema/envelope.schema.json` is a new-file write, and `sakg/__init__.py` is **not** required for this node (the schema is data, loaded by path). | `sakg/` is outside this session's read-capability. IMPLEMENT confirms; note `I-STORE` — not F-ENVELOPE — owns the `pyproject` package registration. |
| **A2** | `tests/sakg/` does not yet exist and pytest collects it without an `__init__.py` (rootdir-relative collection). | Outside read-capability. If collection fails, IMPLEMENT adds the minimal `__init__.py`; the `accept` command is unchanged either way. |
| **A3** | The repo runs under `uv` with a working `uv run pytest`, as every `accept` command in `SAKG-1-backlog.yaml` presumes. | Presumed from the backlog's own acceptance commands. VERIFIER owns the runtime check. |
| **A4** | Fixture files are counted by `ls .../valid/*.json`, so **only** `.json` files may live in those two directories — no README, no `.gitkeep`, no manifest. | Read directly from the F-ENVELOPE `accept` block. Enforced by test T4. |
| **A5** | `jsonschema >= 4.18` (2020-12 support incl. `FORMAT_CHECKER`) is available, or IMPLEMENT adds it to the dev dependency group. | `pyproject.toml` is outside this session's read-capability. If a different validator is already vendored, the schema is unaffected — only the harness import changes. |
| **A6** | Node `id`s use ULIDs, per the literal `sakg://<namespace>/<type>/<ulid>` in §4.2, and the Crockford alphabet is the intended one. | §4.2 says "ulid" without fixing the alphabet. Crockford base32 is the ULID specification's own alphabet; recorded as **OQ-1** if a different form was intended. |
| **A7** | The `<type>` segment of `id` is spelled exactly as the `type` enum value (PascalCase, e.g. `.../TradeOff/...`). | §4.2 gives the template, never a worked example. Chosen for a mechanical X2 check; a lower-kebab convention would require a mapping table and a second source of truth. **OQ-1**. |
| **A8** | `EvidenceRef.kind` is closed at v1 to `{sealed_goal, benchmark, outcome}` — the three bindings ×5 names verbatim ("an outcome, a benchmark, a sealed PAEOS goal"). | ×5 enumerates three; §4.3's extension rule requires a ratified change to add a fourth. If S-PROBE finds a fourth binding class in real sealed goals, this widens by amendment, not by ad-hoc addition. **OQ-3**. |
| **A9** | A `candidate` node may legitimately carry a store-derived `confidence` (fixture V07). | §4.2 does not restrict `confidence` to `canonical`, and §5.1's `min_confidence` filter is applied over `status: [candidate]` opt-in queries, which is only meaningful if candidates are scored. |
